We will need to understand relations between objects in order to simplify it

First relation is Has-a relation the most basic relation between classes is the has-a relation
(also known as the composition), This relation is formed where one object belongs to another object.
For example: A person HAS-A name, bicycles HAVE wheels, etc....
Compositions is implemented in java in a very straight forward manner: using data members so for example:

public class Person {

private String name;
private Person mother;
}

Is-a relation, consider a class that is more specific version of an existing class, A student is a person
students share the features of persons, but they have additional things that a common person doesn't have
in other words: Every student is a person but not every person is a student.

